From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrii Kuiukoff <andros.ua@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 20:41:22 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drivers: mtd: parsers: add mtd-extend-to-end property support to ofpart

Add support for a new optional boolean property, "mtd-extend-to-end",
for partitions described by the "fixed-partitions" OF parser.

When it is set on a partition node, the partition size is not taken
from the DT "reg" property but is calculated as the space between the
partition offset and the end of the parent MTD device. The size in
"reg" must be 0 in this case. Parsing fails with an error if a non-zero
size is given together with the property, or if the partition offset
lies beyond the end of the flash.

This allows describing the last partition (typically "ubi") of a board
without hardcoding the flash size, so a single DTS can be used for
boards that ship with different flash chip sizes or whose usable size
changes with bad block management.

Example:

	partition@580000 {
		label = "ubi";
		reg = <0x580000 0x0>;
		mtd-extend-to-end;
	};

The property is ignored by every DTS that does not set it, so other
targets and boards are unaffected. This is an OpenWrt-specific
extension and is not part of the upstream DT bindings.

Based on the MediaTek SDK patch "Add mtd partition extend to end
support" from mtk-openwrt-feeds. Compared to that version, a size
given together with the property is reported with pr_err() instead of
pr_debug(), and a partition offset beyond the end of the flash is
rejected instead of wrapping the size around.

Link: https://github.com/mediatek/mtk-openwrt-feeds/commit/bb965131de6bf87f67128ec7970d956c2b87f465
Signed-off-by: Andrii Kuiukoff <andros.ua@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/mtd/parsers/ofpart_core.c
+++ b/drivers/mtd/parsers/ofpart_core.c
@@ -157,6 +157,17 @@ static int parse_fixed_partitions(struct
 
 		parts[i].offset = of_read_number(reg, a_cells);
 		parts[i].size = of_read_number(reg + a_cells, s_cells);
+		if (of_property_read_bool(pp, "mtd-extend-to-end")) {
+			if (parts[i].size) {
+				pr_err("partition len must be 0 if using mtd-extend-to-end.\n");
+				goto ofpart_fail;
+			}
+			if (parts[i].offset >= master->size) {
+				pr_err("partition offset is beyond the end of flash.\n");
+				goto ofpart_fail;
+			}
+			parts[i].size = master->size - parts[i].offset;
+		}
 		parts[i].of_node = pp;
 
 		partname = of_get_property(pp, "label", &len);
